{"id":"aneurysm","cards":[{"id":"aneury7c369eee","l":1,"f":"<b>Aneurysm</b> — Definition?","b":"Localized arterial dilatation <b>≥50% greater</b> than the adjacent normal vessel diameter","c":"Definition & Classification"},{"id":"aneury00b6ac8a","l":1,"f":"<b>Arteriomegaly</b> — Definition?","b":"<b>Diffuse</b> arterial enlargement — not a focal aneurysm","c":"Definition & Classification"},{"id":"aneury7d2b4213","l":1,"f":"<b>Term AAA</b> — Definition?","b":"Abdominal aortic diameter <b>≥3 cm</b>","c":"Definition & Classification"},{"id":"aneury111dbaa5","l":1,"f":"<b>True aneurysm</b> — Wall?","b":"Involves <b>all 3 layers</b> — intima, media, adventitia","c":"Definition & Classification"},{"id":"aneury2287319e","l":1,"f":"<b>False aneurysm (pseudoaneurysm)</b> — Wall?","b":"Wall <b>disruption</b>; the sac lacks the 3 arterial wall layers","c":"Definition & Classification"},{"id":"aneuryf9fd9796","l":1,"f":"<b>True aneurysm</b> — Mechanism?","b":"Dilatation of a weakened but intact wall","c":"Definition & Classification"},{"id":"aneury443afc72","l":1,"f":"<b>False aneurysm (pseudoaneurysm)</b> — Mechanism?","b":"Blood escapes through the defect into a <b>contained</b> <b>sac</b>","c":"Definition & Classification"},{"id":"aneury3438d977","l":1,"f":"<b>True aneurysm</b> — Typical cause?","b":"Degenerative (most), genetic, inflammatory, infective","c":"Definition & Classification"},{"id":"aneury4738c64e","l":1,"f":"<b>False aneurysm (pseudoaneurysm)</b> — Typical cause?","b":"<b>Trauma</b> or <b>arterial puncture</b> (e.g., femoral catheterization)","c":"Definition & Classification"},{"id":"aneuryefc9472d","l":1,"f":"<b>True aneurysm</b> — Shape?","b":"<b>Fusiform</b> (circumferential) or <b>saccular</b> (one- sided outpouching)","c":"Definition & Classification"},{"id":"aneurya015ea95","l":1,"f":"<b>False aneurysm (pseudoaneurysm)</b> — Shape?","b":"Sac connected to the artery by a <b>neck</b>","c":"Definition & Classification"},{"id":"aneury4e6336cb","l":1,"f":"<b>True aneurysm</b> — Telling apart?","b":"May look identical clinically → differentiate by <b>imaging</b> or <b>intra-operative findings</b>","c":"Definition & Classification"},{"id":"aneury7f5ab367","l":1,"f":"<b>Degenerative most common</b> — Mechanism?","b":"Weakened <b>elastic lamina &amp; media</b>; ↑ <b>protease</b> activity → collagen/elastin degradation, compounded by pulsatile pressure &amp; altered hemodynamics","c":"Etiology"},{"id":"aneuryb0df3408","l":1,"f":"<b>Degenerative most common</b> — Key associations &amp; clues?","b":"Accounts for most aneurysms","c":"Etiology"},{"id":"aneuryb2a43cc7","l":1,"f":"<b>Genetic / connective tissue</b> — Mechanism?","b":"Inherited structural defects of the arterial wall","c":"Etiology"},{"id":"aneuryd13758ba","l":1,"f":"<b>Genetic / connective tissue</b> — Key associations &amp; clues?","b":"<b>Marfan</b> syndrome · <b>Ehlers-Danlos</b> syndrome","c":"Etiology"},{"id":"aneury8b767adb","l":1,"f":"<b>Inflammatory non-infectious</b> — Mechanism?","b":"Lymphocyte &amp; plasma-cell infiltration → protease release → wall destruction","c":"Etiology"},{"id":"aneury2b49f523","l":1,"f":"<b>Inflammatory non-infectious</b> — Key associations &amp; clues?","b":"Inflammatory disorders (e.g., arthritis) or adjacent inflammation (e.g., <b>chronic</b> <b>pancreatitis</b>); wall looks <b>thickened &amp; whitish</b>","c":"Etiology"},{"id":"aneuryf8161e21","l":1,"f":"<b>Infectious mycotic</b> — Mechanism?","b":"Bacterial infection of the wall → inflammation &amp; progressive wall destruction","c":"Etiology"},{"id":"aneury6aa6269e","l":1,"f":"<b>Infectious mycotic</b> — Key associations &amp; clues?","b":"<b>Salmonella</b> (classic) · <b>Brucella</b> (Saudi Arabia — unpasteurized milk/dairy) · any artery, esp. the <b>aorta</b> · <b>fever</b> common","c":"Etiology"},{"id":"aneurye1d85fe9","l":1,"f":"<b>Other</b> — Mechanism?","b":"Congenital/hereditary abnormalities · <b>post-stenotic dilatation</b> · post-dissection aneurysmal degeneration · trauma · <b>iatrogenic</b> arterial injury","c":"Etiology"},{"id":"aneuryf61205ef","l":2,"f":"Most common site of abdominal aortic aneurysm","b":"<b>infrarenal</b> aorta (answer recalled without the question)","c":"Distribution & Natural History"},{"id":"aneury78fd3a34","l":2,"f":"The most common presentation of AAA","b":"<b>incidental</b> finding","c":"Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm (AAA)"},{"id":"aneury089d22f2","l":2,"f":"A pulsating abdominal mass (in the acute setting) indicates","b":"<b>rupture of an AAA</b>","c":"Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm (AAA)"},{"id":"aneurydbd6ca12","l":2,"f":"Incidental aneurysm managed <b>conservatively</b>","b":"<b>4 cm</b>","c":"Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm (AAA)"},{"id":"aneury1d9ea2fe","l":1,"f":"<b>Ultrasound</b> — Role?","b":"<b>Screening of choice</b>; rapid <b>bedside</b> check in suspected rupture","c":"Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm (AAA)"},{"id":"aneury689583ef","l":1,"f":"<b>Ultrasound</b> — Strengths?","b":"Inexpensive, readily available, <b>no</b> <b>radiation</b>, sensitive for dilatation; may show the aneurysm + associated fluid","c":"Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm (AAA)"},{"id":"aneury67e44d05","l":1,"f":"<b>Ultrasound</b> — Limitations?","b":"<b>Obesity</b> and <b>bowel gas</b> reduce accuracy","c":"Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm (AAA)"},{"id":"aneurye9b1eb9b","l":1,"f":"<b>CT / CTA</b> — Role?","b":"Diagnosis, anatomy &amp; <b>operative planning</b>","c":"Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm (AAA)"},{"id":"aneury51e231ad","l":1,"f":"<b>CT / CTA</b> — Strengths?","b":"Diameter, shape, <b>mural thrombus</b>, normal proximal/distal vessels, branches, adjacent structures, renal anatomy, vascular anomalies","c":"Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm (AAA)"},{"id":"aneury0c2f52be","l":1,"f":"<b>CT / CTA</b> — Limitations?","b":"Measure <b>perpendicular to the</b> <b>centerline</b> — oblique sections overestimate","c":"Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm (AAA)"},{"id":"aneury6660242f","l":1,"f":"<b>Conventional angiography</b> — Role?","b":"Mainly <b>during</b> <b>intervention</b>","c":"Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm (AAA)"},{"id":"aneurydbe6b081","l":1,"f":"<b>Conventional angiography</b> — Strengths?","b":"Outlines the patent, contrast-filled lumen","c":"Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm (AAA)"},{"id":"aneury6cf74cc7","l":1,"f":"<b>Conventional angiography</b> — Limitations?","b":"<b>Underestimates</b> size (mural thrombus not shown); not for primary diagnosis or diameter","c":"Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm (AAA)"},{"id":"aneuryfa4a89c3","l":1,"f":"<b>EVAR — endovascular aneurysm repair</b> — How?","b":"<b>Stent-graft</b> inside the aorta channels blood through the graft, not the sac. Main body + <b>contralateral limb</b> deployed &amp; connected under <b>fluoroscopy</b> — demanding 3D positioning from 2D X-ray images","c":"Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm (AAA)"},{"id":"aneury92f850c3","l":1,"f":"<b>Open surgical repair</b> — How?","b":"Replace the aneurysmal segment with a sewn-in <b>straight tube</b> or <b>bifurcated graft</b> (5 steps below); <b>transperitoneal</b> or <b>retroperitoneal</b> approach","c":"Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm (AAA)"},{"id":"aneuryeefe1483","l":1,"f":"<b>EVAR — endovascular aneurysm repair</b> — Anatomy needed?","b":"Suitable <b>proximal &amp; distal landing zones</b> (normal vessel above/below) for a secure seal &amp; no endoleak; aortic <b>neck shape</b>, aneurysm anatomy, <b>access vessels</b>","c":"Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm (AAA)"},{"id":"aneury77ce65b4","l":1,"f":"<b>Open surgical repair</b> — Anatomy needed?","b":"Not dependent on landing zones","c":"Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm (AAA)"},{"id":"aneuryc2b7add5","l":1,"f":"<b>EVAR — endovascular aneurysm repair</b> — Advantages?","b":"Smaller incisions, <b>less blood loss</b>, <b>lower</b> <b>perioperative morbidity</b>, shorter hospitalization","c":"Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm (AAA)"},{"id":"aneuryf555d44b","l":1,"f":"<b>Open surgical repair</b> — Advantages?","b":"No reliance on long-term imaging surveillance","c":"Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm (AAA)"},{"id":"aneury06973f38","l":1,"f":"<b>EVAR — endovascular aneurysm repair</b> — Drawbacks?","b":"Graft-related complications; <b>long-term</b> <b>surveillance</b> incl. <b>annual CT</b>","c":"Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm (AAA)"},{"id":"aneury53e46c94","l":1,"f":"<b>Open surgical repair</b> — Drawbacks?","b":"Higher early morbidity; elective mortality ≈ <b>5%</b>","c":"Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm (AAA)"},{"id":"aneurya629463b","l":1,"f":"<b>EVAR — endovascular aneurysm repair</b> — Complications?","b":"General: bleeding, infection, thrombosis Specific: <b>endoleak</b> (persistent flow into the sac), graft/limb occlusion, graft thrombosis, <b>femoral</b> <b>access-site</b> complications","c":"Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm (AAA)"},{"id":"aneury287ae33a","l":1,"f":"<b>Open surgical repair</b> — Complications?","b":"Bleeding, infection, thrombosis · <b>renal</b> <b>failure/ischemia</b> · <b>MI</b> · lower-limb ischemia/limb loss · <b>bowel/colonic ischemia</b> · <b>erectile</b> <b>dysfunction</b> (sympathetic plexus near the bifurcation)","c":"Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm (AAA)"},{"id":"aneury004b1d59","l":2,"f":"Aorto-enteric fistula — the false statement","b":"<b>\"always after surgery for AAA\"</b>","c":"Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm (AAA)"},{"id":"aneury7d38e3e6","l":2,"f":"Size indicating surgery","b":"<b>5.5 cm</b>","c":"Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm (AAA)"},{"id":"aneury8452c288","l":2,"f":"Pulsatile epigastric mass with <b>BP 80/60</b>","b":"keyed <b>immediate laparotomy</b> (straight to theatre — don't delay for CT)","c":"Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm (AAA)"},{"id":"aneury6dbea266","l":1,"f":"<b>AAA</b> — Frequency?","b":"<b>Most common</b> aneurysm (infrarenal aorta)","c":"Thoracic Aortic Aneurysm (TAA)"},{"id":"aneury4aca449b","l":1,"f":"<b>TAA</b> — Frequency?","b":"Less common; rising with <b>aging</b> &amp; more chest imaging","c":"Thoracic Aortic Aneurysm (TAA)"},{"id":"aneuryeba1691f","l":1,"f":"<b>AAA</b> — Who?","b":"Older men; smokers","c":"Thoracic Aortic Aneurysm (TAA)"},{"id":"aneury2553d6f8","l":1,"f":"<b>TAA</b> — Who?","b":"Older; greater <b>male</b> predominance; <b>familial</b> (first- degree relatives)","c":"Thoracic Aortic Aneurysm (TAA)"},{"id":"aneuryb1346761","l":1,"f":"<b>AAA</b> — Causes?","b":"Degenerative most common","c":"Thoracic Aortic Aneurysm (TAA)"},{"id":"aneury50177da1","l":1,"f":"<b>TAA</b> — Causes?","b":"Degenerative most common; <b>post-dissection</b>, connective tissue disorders, autoimmune/inflammatory, infection","c":"Thoracic Aortic Aneurysm (TAA)"},{"id":"aneuryce433877","l":1,"f":"<b>AAA</b> — Risk factors?","b":"Age, male, smoking (pack-years), HTN, CV disease","c":"Thoracic Aortic Aneurysm (TAA)"},{"id":"aneurydea10ec3","l":1,"f":"<b>TAA</b> — Risk factors?","b":"Smoking, <b>alcohol</b>, age, HTN, <b>COPD</b>","c":"Thoracic Aortic Aneurysm (TAA)"},{"id":"aneuryd1788e8a","l":1,"f":"<b>AAA</b> — Rupture risk ↑?","b":"Diameter, growth, smoking, COPD, female sex","c":"Thoracic Aortic Aneurysm (TAA)"},{"id":"aneury81736bc4","l":1,"f":"<b>TAA</b> — Rupture risk ↑?","b":"Diameter, <b>age</b>, growth rate — <b>~1 cm/year</b> is particularly concerning","c":"Thoracic Aortic Aneurysm (TAA)"},{"id":"aneury3db5b233","l":1,"f":"<b>Esophagus</b> — Result?","b":"<b>Dysphagia</b>","c":"Thoracic Aortic Aneurysm (TAA)"},{"id":"aneury1ab4806b","l":1,"f":"<b>Trachea / airways</b> — Result?","b":"Respiratory or irritation symptoms","c":"Thoracic Aortic Aneurysm (TAA)"},{"id":"aneury603109b0","l":1,"f":"<b>Adjacent nerves</b> — Result?","b":"Neurological / <b>voice-related</b> symptoms","c":"Thoracic Aortic Aneurysm (TAA)"},{"id":"aneury0e5f7052","l":2,"f":"Symptom distinguishing a <b>thoracic</b> from an abdominal aneurysm","b":"<b>cough and hoarseness</b> (compression of the airway/recurrent laryngeal nerve)","c":"Thoracic Aortic Aneurysm (TAA)"},{"id":"aneurye21ea534","l":1,"f":"<b>AAA</b> — Imaging?","b":"<b>Ultrasound</b> screens; CTA plans","c":"Thoracic Aortic Aneurysm (TAA)"},{"id":"aneury491e8bf8","l":1,"f":"<b>TAA</b> — Imaging?","b":"<b>CTA</b> (ultrasound limited by thoracic structures)","c":"Thoracic Aortic Aneurysm (TAA)"},{"id":"aneury49b6c918","l":1,"f":"<b>AAA</b> — Repair?","b":"<b>≥5.5 cm</b> men / <b>≥5.0 cm</b> women; symptomatic; rupture; rapid growth","c":"Thoracic Aortic Aneurysm (TAA)"},{"id":"aneurya0b122eb","l":1,"f":"<b>TAA</b> — Repair?","b":"<b>~6 cm</b> (higher morbidity of thoracic repair); symptomatic; rupture; rapid expansion","c":"Thoracic Aortic Aneurysm (TAA)"},{"id":"aneury1173df55","l":1,"f":"<b>AAA</b> — Endovascular?","b":"EVAR","c":"Thoracic Aortic Aneurysm (TAA)"},{"id":"aneury5720a56e","l":1,"f":"<b>TAA</b> — Endovascular?","b":"<b>TEVAR</b> (open or hybrid repair when anatomy requires)","c":"Thoracic Aortic Aneurysm (TAA)"},{"id":"aneury57c46717","l":1,"f":"<b>AAA</b> — Signature risk?","b":"Endoleak (EVAR); bowel/renal ischemia, ED (open)","c":"Thoracic Aortic Aneurysm (TAA)"},{"id":"aneury9f80461b","l":1,"f":"<b>TAA</b> — Signature risk?","b":"<b>Spinal cord ischemia / paraplegia</b>, stroke","c":"Thoracic Aortic Aneurysm (TAA)"},{"id":"aneury78ec2d11","l":1,"f":"<b>US-guided compression</b> — How it works?","b":"Pressure over the <b>neck</b> → interrupts flow → sac thrombosis","c":"Peripheral Arterial Aneurysms"},{"id":"aneuryba129a9e","l":1,"f":"<b>US-guided compression</b> — Best use / caution?","b":"Non-invasive","c":"Peripheral Arterial Aneurysms"},{"id":"aneuryc4cfc85a","l":1,"f":"<b>US-guided thrombin injection</b> — How it works?","b":"Thrombin into the <b>sac</b> → induces clotting","c":"Peripheral Arterial Aneurysms"},{"id":"aneury59de5ce7","l":1,"f":"<b>US-guided thrombin injection</b> — Best use / caution?","b":"Best with a <b>narrow, suitable neck</b>","c":"Peripheral Arterial Aneurysms"},{"id":"aneuryd3d556e8","l":1,"f":"<b>Surgical repair</b> — How it works?","b":"Direct open repair","c":"Peripheral Arterial Aneurysms"},{"id":"aneury43ff9396","l":1,"f":"<b>Surgical repair</b> — Best use / caution?","b":"When percutaneous methods are unsuitable or complications require intervention","c":"Peripheral Arterial Aneurysms"},{"id":"aneurydcd65579","l":1,"f":"<b>Femoral</b> — Frequency?","b":"<b>Most common</b> iatrogenic site","c":"Radial Artery Aneurysms"},{"id":"aneury0533b660","l":1,"f":"<b>Radial</b> — Frequency?","b":"Much less common","c":"Radial Artery Aneurysms"},{"id":"aneury86a44c44","l":1,"f":"<b>Femoral</b> — Why?","b":"<b>Deep</b>, difficult to compress; obesity","c":"Radial Artery Aneurysms"},{"id":"aneuryd160ea55","l":1,"f":"<b>Radial</b> — Why?","b":"<b>Superficial</b>, compressible against bone","c":"Radial Artery Aneurysms"},{"id":"aneury9bec7767","l":1,"f":"<b>Femoral</b> — Special issues?","b":"Mycotic pseudoaneurysm in IV drug users; femoral nerve &amp; venous compression","c":"Radial Artery Aneurysms"},{"id":"aneury46ff16b5","l":1,"f":"<b>Radial</b> — Special issues?","b":"<b>Small caliber</b> → thrombosis; hand relies on ulnar collateral","c":"Radial Artery Aneurysms"},{"id":"aneuryd1a12957","l":1,"f":"<b>Femoral</b> — Prevention / Rx?","b":"<b>US-guided puncture</b>; US compression, thrombin injection or surgery","c":"Radial Artery Aneurysms"},{"id":"aneurydf8c0c8d","l":1,"f":"<b>Radial</b> — Prevention / Rx?","b":"<b>Allen's test</b> → ligate if collateral adequate, otherwise reconstruct","c":"Radial Artery Aneurysms"},{"id":"aneuryb9e264c8","l":2,"f":"Incidental AAA — indication for surgery","b":"<b>symptomatic</b> (not 3.5–4 cm or hypertension)","c":"Visceral Artery Aneurysms"},{"id":"aneurye9f0f2b1","l":1,"f":"<b>Splenic</b> — Frequency?","b":"<b>Most common</b> (~60%) · women","c":"Visceral Artery Aneurysms"},{"id":"aneury6bba6ae5","l":1,"f":"<b>Hepatic</b> — Frequency?","b":"2nd · <b>men</b>","c":"Visceral Artery Aneurysms"},{"id":"aneury21fcbdf4","l":1,"f":"<b>SMA</b> — Frequency?","b":"Uncommon","c":"Visceral Artery Aneurysms"},{"id":"aneury3cd564b5","l":1,"f":"<b>Renal</b> — Frequency?","b":"Relatively uncommon · women","c":"Visceral Artery Aneurysms"},{"id":"aneury02f56fd0","l":1,"f":"<b>Splenic</b> — Hallmark?","b":"FMD; portal HTN; <b>pregnancy rupture</b>","c":"Visceral Artery Aneurysms"},{"id":"aneury094a3321","l":1,"f":"<b>Hepatic</b> — Hallmark?","b":"<b>Hemobilia</b> triad; rupture mortality ~35%","c":"Visceral Artery Aneurysms"},{"id":"aneury752b09ce","l":1,"f":"<b>SMA</b> — Hallmark?","b":"Often <b>mycotic</b>; bowel ischemia, fistula","c":"Visceral Artery Aneurysms"},{"id":"aneury9b0e8434","l":1,"f":"<b>Renal</b> — Hallmark?","b":"Saccular at 1st bifurcation; <b>renovascular HTN</b>","c":"Visceral Artery Aneurysms"},{"id":"aneury565ce806","l":1,"f":"<b>Splenic</b> — Repair when?","b":"&gt;2 cm · symptomatic · childbearing age","c":"Visceral Artery Aneurysms"},{"id":"aneuryfd2e3068","l":1,"f":"<b>Hepatic</b> — Repair when?","b":"Per site &amp; anatomy","c":"Visceral Artery Aneurysms"},{"id":"aneuryb3507977","l":1,"f":"<b>SMA</b> — Repair when?","b":"Per location &amp; branch importance","c":"Visceral Artery Aneurysms"},{"id":"aneuryef3d01e9","l":1,"f":"<b>Renal</b> — Repair when?","b":"&gt;2 cm · childbearing age · uncontrolled HTN · symptomatic","c":"Visceral Artery Aneurysms"},{"id":"aneurycaf31bbe","l":1,"f":"<b>Splenic</b> — Key Rx point?","b":"Coils / covered stent; hilar → splenectomy","c":"Visceral Artery Aneurysms"},{"id":"aneury30d25a51","l":1,"f":"<b>Hepatic</b> — Key Rx point?","b":"Ligation OK if collaterals (portal flow)","c":"Visceral Artery Aneurysms"},{"id":"aneurya777869b","l":1,"f":"<b>SMA</b> — Key Rx point?","b":"No endografts in infection; keep major branches","c":"Visceral Artery Aneurysms"},{"id":"aneuryb792c79b","l":1,"f":"<b>Renal</b> — Key Rx point?","b":"Stent-graft or reconstruction; hilar = complex","c":"Visceral Artery Aneurysms"},{"id":"aneury88cfc5fa","l":1,"f":"<b>Aneurysm AAA</b> — Size trigger?","b":"<b>≥5.5 cm</b> men · <b>≥5.0 cm</b> women","c":"High-Yield Synthesis"},{"id":"aneury04a0cce8","l":1,"f":"<b>Aneurysm AAA</b> — Other triggers?","b":"Symptomatic (urgent) · ruptured (immediate) · growth ≥0.5 cm/6 mo or ≥1 cm/yr","c":"High-Yield Synthesis"},{"id":"aneury19f1b3b1","l":1,"f":"<b>Aneurysm AAA</b> — Dominant danger?","b":"Rupture","c":"High-Yield Synthesis"},{"id":"aneury755f6da6","l":1,"f":"<b>Aneurysm TAA</b> — Size trigger?","b":"<b>~6 cm</b>","c":"High-Yield Synthesis"},{"id":"aneury582d007c","l":1,"f":"<b>Aneurysm TAA</b> — Other triggers?","b":"Symptomatic · ruptured · rapid expansion (~1 cm/yr)","c":"High-Yield Synthesis"},{"id":"aneuryac195e96","l":1,"f":"<b>Aneurysm TAA</b> — Dominant danger?","b":"Rupture; spinal cord ischemia after repair","c":"High-Yield Synthesis"},{"id":"aneury603e67df","l":1,"f":"<b>Popliteal</b> — Size trigger?","b":"<b>~2–2.5 cm</b>","c":"High-Yield Synthesis"},{"id":"aneury35a37b20","l":1,"f":"<b>Popliteal</b> — Other triggers?","b":"Symptomatic: embolization, thrombosis, compression","c":"High-Yield Synthesis"},{"id":"aneuryc3377b03","l":1,"f":"<b>Popliteal</b> — Dominant danger?","b":"Thrombosis/embolization → limb loss","c":"High-Yield Synthesis"},{"id":"aneuryc638db7a","l":1,"f":"<b>Splenic</b> — Size trigger?","b":"<b>&gt;2 cm</b>","c":"High-Yield Synthesis"},{"id":"aneuryd539557d","l":1,"f":"<b>Splenic</b> — Other triggers?","b":"Symptomatic · woman of childbearing age","c":"High-Yield Synthesis"},{"id":"aneurye12c7a09","l":1,"f":"<b>Splenic</b> — Dominant danger?","b":"Rupture in pregnancy (maternal ~75%, fetal ~90% mortality)","c":"High-Yield Synthesis"},{"id":"aneury37d02a29","l":1,"f":"<b>Renal IMAGING OF CHOICE</b> — Size trigger?","b":"<b>&gt;2 cm</b>","c":"High-Yield Synthesis"},{"id":"aneury32e81676","l":1,"f":"<b>Renal IMAGING OF CHOICE</b> — Other triggers?","b":"Childbearing age · uncontrolled renovascular HTN · symptomatic/↓ renal function","c":"High-Yield Synthesis"},{"id":"aneuryd16cfb3a","l":1,"f":"<b>Renal IMAGING OF CHOICE</b> — Dominant danger?","b":"Renovascular HTN; rupture concern in pregnancy","c":"High-Yield Synthesis"},{"id":"aneurybf9a580e","l":1,"f":"<b>AAA screening</b> — Best test?","b":"<b>Ultrasound</b>","c":"High-Yield Synthesis"},{"id":"aneury4689ccf2","l":1,"f":"<b>AAA screening</b> — Why / watch out?","b":"Cheap, no radiation, sensitive — limited by obesity &amp; bowel gas","c":"High-Yield Synthesis"},{"id":"aneury3147cf8e","l":1,"f":"<b>AAA diagnosis &amp; planning</b> — Best test?","b":"<b>CTA</b>","c":"High-Yield Synthesis"},{"id":"aneury56196af2","l":1,"f":"<b>AAA diagnosis &amp; planning</b> — Why / watch out?","b":"Diameter, thrombus, landing zones, branches — measure perpendicular to centerline","c":"High-Yield Synthesis"},{"id":"aneury8cfbd1a3","l":1,"f":"<b>Suspected rupture</b> — Best test?","b":"Unstable: <b>bedside US</b> Stable: <b>CTA</b>","c":"High-Yield Synthesis"},{"id":"aneurycb62c130","l":1,"f":"<b>Suspected rupture</b> — Why / watch out?","b":"Rapid bedside assessment; CTA only if it won't delay definitive treatment","c":"High-Yield Synthesis"},{"id":"aneury9012a2dd","l":1,"f":"<b>Scenario TAA</b> — Best test?","b":"<b>CTA</b>","c":"High-Yield Synthesis"},{"id":"aneuryd8decf6e","l":1,"f":"<b>Scenario TAA</b> — Why / watch out?","b":"Ultrasound limited by thoracic structures","c":"High-Yield Synthesis"},{"id":"aneury47ca82ba","l":1,"f":"<b>Peripheral (popliteal, femoral)</b> — Best test?","b":"<b>Duplex ultrasound</b>","c":"High-Yield Synthesis"},{"id":"aneury1bc01edf","l":1,"f":"<b>Peripheral (popliteal, femoral)</b> — Why / watch out?","b":"Superficial vessels; distinguishes true vs pseudoaneurysm","c":"High-Yield Synthesis"},{"id":"aneurye869b71a","l":1,"f":"<b>SMA / renal</b> — Best test?","b":"<b>CT / CTA</b>","c":"High-Yield Synthesis"},{"id":"aneury4d122cb7","l":1,"f":"<b>SMA / renal</b> — Why / watch out?","b":"Bowel gas limits ultrasound; CTA for renal surveillance","c":"High-Yield Synthesis"},{"id":"aneuryd2696bae","l":1,"f":"<b>Conventional angiography</b> — Best test?","b":"During intervention","c":"High-Yield Synthesis"},{"id":"aneury68246801","l":1,"f":"<b>Conventional angiography</b> — Why / watch out?","b":"<b>Underestimates</b> size — shows the flowing lumen only","c":"High-Yield Synthesis"},{"id":"aneurya24cb800","l":2,"f":"Investigation used to diagnose an aortic aneurysm","b":"keyed <b>duplex ultrasound</b> (the screening/diagnostic test; CT then plans repair)","c":"High-Yield Synthesis"}]}